@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title UCT — Bandit-Based Monte-Carlo Tree Search
' Paper: Bandit Based Monte-Carlo Planning
' URL:   https://doi.org/10.1007/11871842_29
' Level: 1

component "Selection\nUCB1 down the known tree" as SEL <<app>>
component "Expansion\nadd one child node" as EXP <<app>>
cloud     "Simulation\nplay out to a result" as SIM <<cloud>>
component "Backpropagation\nupdate visits and value" as BACK <<async>>
database  "Search tree\nasymmetric, grows where it matters" as TREE <<db>>

SEL ARROW_MAIN EXP : reached a leaf
EXP ARROW_CLOUD SIM : from the new node
SIM ARROW_MAIN BACK : outcome
BACK ARROW_QUEUE TREE : statistics per node
TREE ARROW_MAIN SEL : next iteration

note bottom of SEL
  **The idea is to treat each node as a bandit.**
  UCB1 balances exploiting the child with the best
  observed value against exploring the one with few
  visits, so the tree grows **asymmetrically** —
  deep along promising lines, shallow elsewhere. No
  evaluation function is required: a random playout
  supplies the signal, and the estimate improves
  with samples.
  ----
  **Two assumptions to check before reaching for it.**
  The cited paper analyses UCT for **MDP planning**;
  the familiar game-tree form adds the assumption that
  turns //alternate//. Simultaneous moves break that
  added assumption. Separately, a playout must start
  from the //true// state — hidden state breaks that, and
  playouts must then run in sampled worlds
  (""../imperfect-information-games/determinization.puml"").
end note
@enduml
